/*
 * Package tui: the entry file of the terminal user interface library.
 *
 * tui is a retained-mode TUI library. Applications build a tree of
 * long-lived widgets, mutate their state, and let a Screen turn terminal
 * input into events and widget output into frames. It sits on top of
 * std/term and never writes escape sequences of its own.
 *
 * It started as basalam, written by Parsa
 * (https://github.com/curedbylethe/basalam), and moved into the standard
 * library with its resize watcher's signal half as os.signal.
 *
 * Consumers pull the whole package in with one line:
 *
 *     import tui
 *
 * Every .salam file in std/tui/ belongs to the package, so the sibling
 * files below are loaded automatically:
 *
 *     rect.salam     geometry: Rect and Point (cell coordinates)
 *     event.salam    Event, the value input arrives as, and its kinds
 *     buffer.salam   Buffer and Cell, the grid widgets draw into
 *     color.salam    the Color value type and its raw SGR encoding
 *     style.salam    the Style value type, merge, equality and SGR emission
 *     border.salam   box-drawing border rings and the DrawBorder helper
 *     panel.salam    the Panel decorator: one framed child, its inset and title
 *     modal.salam    the Modal overlay: a dialog over a dim scrim, with focus and Esc
 *     widget.salam   the Widget interface and BaseWidget defaults
 *     layout.salam   the Row, Column, Grid and Stack containers
 *     width.salam    the one cell-width rule: codepoint width, string width, cell clipping
 *     text.salam     the Text widget and the pure line rules it draws through
 *     input.salam    the Input widget: single-line text entry with a caret
 *     list.salam     the List widget: single-selection scrollable list
 *     button.salam   the Button widget: one-row action button with on_click
 *     checkbox.salam the Checkbox widget: one-row boolean toggle
 *     progress.salam the Progress widget: one-row buffer-drawn progress bar
 *     table.salam    the Table widget: a non-focusable grid; TableView: its scrollable variant
 *     separator.salam the Separator widget: one-line horizontal or vertical rule
 *     tree.salam     the widget registry (IDs, parents) and event bubbling
 *     screen.salam   Screen: terminal session, colour tier detection, input thread, event loop
 *     focus.salam    spatial focus search (Nearest) and the Dir* constants
 *     keymap.salam   the opt-in key and key-sequence binding table
 *
 * Keep test programs and examples out of this directory: anything placed
 * here becomes part of the package.
 */

@en "tui"
@fa "رابط پایانه"
package tui

